# Local Foundry test fixtures. Tracked by the parent repo; this directory is not its own repo.
#
# EXCLUDED - must never enter this repository:
#   * foundry-v*     Commercial, license-keyed Foundry VTT binaries.
#   * data-v*/Config Holds the Foundry licence key (license.json) and the admin secret.
#   * Logs/*.log etc Runtime log output, rewritten on every boot.
#   * Data/modules   Third-party modules the user installs, not fixtures.
#   * Data/assets    User-uploaded files.
#   * node_modules, dist

foundry-v*/
*/node_modules/
*/dist/

# Everything inside a data dir is machine-local unless re-opened below. This matches the
# *contents* rather than the data dir itself: git cannot re-include anything beneath an
# excluded directory, so excluding `data-v*/` would make every negation below unreachable.
data-v*/*
!data-v*/Data/
!data-v*/Logs/

# User downloads inside Data are not fixtures.
data-v*/Data/modules/
data-v*/Data/assets/

# Runtime output in Logs. The world is excluded from this: Foundry v13 keeps its world under
# Logs/worlds, while v14 uses Data/worlds, so both layouts have to stay tracked.
data-v*/Logs/*
!data-v*/Logs/worlds/

# The fixtures themselves - the installed-system links and the frozen test worlds - are
# included by default once the directories above are re-opened.

*.swp
.idea
.vs
.vscode
.DS_Store